        "[DOC_ID:query-cache] Query reuse  \nENABLE_QUERIES_CACHE stores web-search queries on request state so later file retrieval in the same combined chat request can reuse them. Repeating the standalone query endpoint cannot exercise this optimization.",
        "[DOC_ID:resume-cache] Paid output cache  \nCache every paid response under a stable key that binds condition, dataset hash, endpoint, and payload. Write the cache atomically before the append-only action manifest. On resume, a valid cache alone must prevent a repeated provider call.",
        "[DOC_ID:wire-capture] Proxy evidence  \nCapture redacted provider request and response bodies, actual reported input, output, and cached tokens, completion latency, and all budget mutations. For nonstreaming task calls, mark time to first token unavailable rather than relabeling response time."
